// Objective - DefeatDuray 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Description :
"P354543703" "Defeat Duray"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Script Variable BOSS_1_DISPLAYNAME :
"P219875924" "X-Type 2"
// Script Variable BOSS1_DISPLAYINFO :
"P854248332" "This cyborg is much more advanced than the Type 53. Neuron has managed to maintain most of the subject's personality while still boosting their physical prowess."
// Script Variable BOSS_1_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P3516855958" "<shout>Defend the Colonel!"
// Script Variable BOSS_2_DISPLAYNAME :
"P641096087" "X-Type 1"
// Script Variable BOSS2_DISPLAYINFO :
"P635029720" "This cyborg is much more advanced than the Type 22. Neuron has managed to maintain most of the subject's personality while still boosting their physical prowess."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1549322156" "You and Crow defeated Duray and rescued the two Arachnos Blood Widows, Dahlia and Scarlet, after their stalemate with Maelstrom."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1719378428" "Dahlia and Scarlet are reporting back to their master, some guy named <color red>Recluse</color>. Dahlia told me that Maelstrom has grown more powerful in his time here, and that Arachnos will have to analyze the situation before they commit to aiding us. She told me that if I ever made it to the Rogue Isles that she would find me. Part of me thinks that may have been a warning.<br><br>I'm conflicted, {HeroName}. Duray is dead, but my vengeance is not yet complete.<br><br>Neuron has turned my old comrades into abominations. I saw those men dead, {HeroName}, abandoned in the tunnels like refuse. And yet today there they were, fighting, talking, following Duray's orders like nothing happened.<br><br>I don't seek to avenge them any longer, {HeroName}. My vengeance is for all those other pathetic creatures that Neuron has dumped into the tunnels. If there is hope for them, then the Resistance has found the army it needs to overthrow Tyrant and his cronies."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
